     373: StartTextStyle { kind: Bold, id: None }
     374: LineBreak
     375: EndTextStyle
     376: StartTextStyle { kind: Bold, id: None }
     377: Text { content: "Radiation Exposure Compensation Act Trust Fund" }
     378: EndTextStyle
     379: EndParagraph
     380: StartParagraph { alignment: Some(Center), id: None }
     381: EndParagraph
     382: StartParagraph { alignment: Some(Center), id: None }
     383: StartTextStyle { kind: Bold, id: None }
     384: Text { content: "Overview" }
     385: EndTextStyle
     386: EndParagraph
     387: StartParagraph { alignment: None, id: None }
     388: EndParagraph
     389: StartParagraph { alignment: Some(Justify), id: None }
     390: Text { content: "On October 5, 1990, Congress passed the Radiation Exposure Compensation Act (RECA or the Act).  The Act offers an apology and monetary compensation to individuals who contracted certain cancers and other serious diseases as a result of their exposure to radiation released during above-ground atmospheric nuclear weapons tests or as a result of their occupational exposure while employed in the uranium industry during the build-up to the Cold War.  This unique program was designed as an alternative to litigation in that the statutory criteria do not require claimants to establish causality.  Specifically, if the claimant can satisfy the requirements outlined in the statute, which include demonstrating that he or she contracted a compensable disease after working or residing in a designated location for a specified period of time, he or she qualifies for compensation.  The amount of the award is statutorily prescribed and ranges from $50,000 to $100,000, depending on claimant category.  Congress charged the Attorney General with responsibility for adjudicating claims under the Act.  " }
     391: EndParagraph
     392: StartParagraph { alignment: Some(Justify), id: None }
     393: EndParagraph
     394: StartParagraph { alignment: Some(Justify), id: None }
     395: Text { content: "The Department of Justice (DOJ) established the Radiation Exposure Compensation Program (the Program) within the Civil Division.  The Program commenced operations in April 1992.  Since its inception, 27,492 claims have been filed and over $1.2 billion has been awarded to 18,885 claimants (as of January 6, 2008).  " }
     396: EndParagraph
     397: StartParagraph { alignment: Some(Justify), id: None }
     398: EndParagraph
     399: StartParagraph { alignment: Some(Justify), id: None }
     400: Text { content: "The RECA Program was evaluated with OMB’s Program Assessment Rating Tool (PART) during FY 2006.  See page six for more information on the results of this evaluation. " }
     401: EndParagraph
     402: StartParagraph { alignment: Some(Justify), id: None }
     403: EndParagraph
     404: StartParagraph { alignment: Some(Justify), id: None }
     405: Text { content: "Electronic copies of DOJ’s Congressional Budget Justifications and Capital Asset Plan and Business Case exhibits can be viewed or downloaded from the Internet using the Internet address:  " }
     406: StartLink { href: "http://www.usdoj.gov/jmd/2009justification/", id: None, title: None }
     407: Text { content: "http://www.usdoj.gov/jmd/2009justification/" }
     408: EndLink
     409: Text { content: ". " }
     410: EndParagraph
     411: StartParagraph { alignment: Some(Justify), id: None }
     412: EndParagraph
     413: StartParagraph { alignment: Some(Center), id: None }
     414: StartTextStyle { kind: Bold, id: None }
     415: Text { content: "Program Description" }
     416: EndTextStyle
     417: EndParagraph
     418: StartParagraph { alignment: None, id: None }
     419: EndParagraph
     420: StartParagraph { alignment: Some(Justify), id: None }
     421: Text { content: "The Program office is located in " }
     422: Text { content: "Washington" }
     423: Text { content: ", " }
     424: Text { content: "D.C." }
     425: Text { content: " and is administered by a staff of attorneys, claims examiners, and an office assistant within the Civil Division’s Torts Branch.  The support staff reviews claims packages, assists claimants with their applications, and manages physical case files.  The Civil Division strives to process and resolve claims fairly and efficiently. " }
     426: EndParagraph
     427: StartParagraph { alignment: Some(Justify), id: None }
     428: EndParagraph
     429: StartParagraph { alignment: Some(Center), id: None }
     430: StartTextStyle { kind: Bold, id: None }
     431: StartTextStyle { kind: TextColor(Rgb { b: 153, g: 102, r: 0 }), id: None }
     432: Text { content: "Background" }
     433: EndTextStyle
     434: EndTextStyle
     435: EndParagraph
     436: StartParagraph { alignment: Some(Center), id: None }
     437: EndParagraph
     438: StartParagraph { alignment: Some(Justify), id: None }
     439: Text { content: "From 1945 through 1962, the " }
     440: Text { content: "United States" }
     441: Text { content: " conducted extensive atmospheric atomic weapons testing as it developed and built the effective arsenal that became the cornerstone of the Nation’s Cold War security strategy.  Critical to the production of atomic weapons was the mining, milling, and transporting of uranium ore by the tens of thousands of individuals employed in that industry.  Many people exposed to radiation resulting from the nuclear weapons development and testing subsequently developed serious diseases, including various types of cancer.  In order to establish a procedure to make partial restitution to these individuals, the Radiation Exposure Compensation Act was enacted in 1990." }
     442: EndParagraph
     443: StartParagraph { alignment: None, id: None }
     444: EndParagraph
     445: StartParagraph { alignment: Some(Justify), id: None }
     446: Text { content: "The Act established monetary compensation for specified diseases in three defined populations:  underground uranium miners, who receive $100,000; individuals present at test site locations, who receive $75,000 (on-site participants); and individuals who lived downwind of the Nevada Test Site, who receive $50,000 (downwinders).  The map below shows the geographic areas covered by the Act.  Although the vast majority of claims are filed by people living in the Four Corners Region (Utah, Colorado, New Mexico, and Arizona), the Program has awarded compensation to individuals residing in every state as well as several foreign countries.  " }
     447: EndParagraph
     448: StartParagraph { alignment: Some(Justify), id: None }
     449: EndParagraph
     450: StartParagraph { alignment: Some(Justify), id: None }
     451: EndParagraph
     452: StartParagraph { alignment: Some(Justify), id: None }
     453: EndParagraph
     454: StartParagraph { alignment: Some(Justify), id: None }
     455: Text { content: "On July 10, 2000, amendments to RECA (2000 Amendments) were enacted that markedly expanded the scope of the Program.  Major changes included the creation of new categories of beneficiaries (above-ground uranium miners, uranium mill workers, and ore transporters) who receive $100,000 in compensation; the expansion of eligible diseases, geographic areas, and time period; and the reduction in the radiation exposure threshold that miners must meet to receive compensation.  As a result, there was a flood of new claim filings and a sharp rise in monetary awards.  " }
     456: EndParagraph
     457: StartParagraph { alignment: Some(Center), id: None }
     458: EndParagraph
     459: StartParagraph { alignment: Some(Center), id: None }
     460: StartTextStyle { kind: Bold, id: None }
     461: StartTextStyle { kind: TextColor(Rgb { b: 153, g: 102, r: 0 }), id: None }
     462: Text { content: "Scientific Studies" }
     463: EndTextStyle
     464: EndTextStyle
     465: EndParagraph
     466: StartParagraph { alignment: Some(Center), id: None }
     467: EndParagraph
     468: StartParagraph { alignment: Some(Justify), id: None }
     469: Text { content: "The National Research Council of the National Academ" }
     470: Text { content: "y" }
     471: Text { content: " of Science" }
     472: Text { content: "s (NAS)" }
     473: Text { content: " published a study in April 2005 concerning possible changes to RECA, particularly whether other groups of individuals or additional geographic regions or diseases should be covered.  The report conclude" }
     474: Text { content: "d" }
     475: Text { content: " that" }
     476: Text { content: ":" }
     477: Text { content: " 1)\u{a0}based on current scientific evidence, no additional diseases\u{a0}should be included under RECA; 2) further study\u{a0}should be conducted to assess\u{a0}all\u{a0}radionuclides and radiogenic diseases to establish a probability of causation model t" }
     478: Text { content: "o" }
     479: Text { content: " determine possible expansion of compensation beyond current geographic boundaries; and 3) Congress " }
     480: Text { content: "should " }
     481: Text { content: "set new eligibility criteria based on a scientific assessment." }
     482: EndParagraph
     483: StartParagraph { alignment: Some(Center), id: None }
     484: StartTextStyle { kind: Bold, id: None }
     485: StartTextStyle { kind: TextColor(Rgb { b: 153, g: 102, r: 0 }), id: None }
     486: Text { content: "  " }
     487: EndTextStyle
     488: EndTextStyle
     489: EndParagraph
     490: StartParagraph { alignment: Some(Center), id: None }
     491: StartTextStyle { kind: Bold, id: None }
     492: StartTextStyle { kind: TextColor(Rgb { b: 153, g: 102, r: 0 }), id: None }
     493: Text { content: "Proposed Legislation" }
     494: EndTextStyle
     495: EndTextStyle
     496: EndParagraph
     497: StartParagraph { alignment: Some(Center), id: None }
     498: EndParagraph
     499: StartParagraph { alignment: Some(Justify), id: None }
     500: Text { content: "As a result of this " }
     501: Text { content: "study" }
     502: Text { content: ", regardless of the findings, there " }
     503: Text { content: "was initially" }
     504: Text { content: " a rise in the number of claims filed due to increased awareness of the Program within affected communities." }
     505: Text { content: "  The study also spurred congressional interest." }
     506: Text { content: "  " }
     507: Text { content: "Legislation to amend RECA has been introduced in the current session of Congress.  On August 1, 2007, Senators Craig, Crapo, Baucus, and Tester sponsored legislation (S. 1917) to add the states of " }
     508: Text { content: "Idaho" }
     509: Text { content: " and " }
     510: Text { content: "Montana" }
     511: Text { content: " as affected “downwinder” areas.  On August 3, 2007, Congresswoman Bordallo introduced a bill (H.R. 3379) to include the " }
     512: Text { content: "Territory" }
     513: Text { content: " of " }
     514: Text { content: "Guam" }
     515: Text { content: ".  " }
     516: Text { content: "Current workload and funding projections do not account for the possible impact of any scientific studies or substantive statutory changes." }
     517: EndParagraph
     518: StartParagraph { alignment: Some(Justify), id: None }
     519: EndParagraph
     520: StartParagraph { alignment: Some(Center), id: None }
     521: StartTextStyle { kind: Bold, id: None }
     522: StartTextStyle { kind: TextColor(Rgb { b: 153, g: 102, r: 0 }), id: None }
     523: Text { content: "Government Accountability Office (GAO) Audit" }
     524: EndTextStyle
     525: EndTextStyle
     526: EndParagraph
     527: StartParagraph { alignment: Some(Justify), id: None }
     528: StartTextStyle { kind: Bold, id: None }
     529: StartTextStyle { kind: TextColor(Rgb { b: 153, g: 102, r: 0 }), id: None }
     530: Text { content: "\u{a0}  " }
     531: EndTextStyle
     532: EndTextStyle
     533: EndParagraph
     534: StartParagraph { alignment: Some(Justify), id: None }
     535: Text { content: "Since enactment of the 2000 Amendments, which included a provision requiring GAO to report to Congress every 18 months on the administration of the Program, there have been four audit reports.\u{a0}\u{a0}The\u{a0}most recent report on Program administration, dated September 17, 200" }
     536: Text { content: "7" }
     537: Text { content: ", was very favorable.\u{a0} The report noted that $1.2 billion was paid to eligible claimants between 1992 and June 2007" }
     538: Text { content: " and " }
     539: Text { content: "almost half\u{a0}of that amount was paid to downwinder claimants.\u{a0} GAO also determined that average processing times for each individual category of claims have decreased over the last four years.\u{a0} No negative findings were made and no response was required by the Department." }
     540: Text { content: "  The FY 2008 Omnibus Appropriations Bill, section 1502(g), struck this statutory reporting requirement." }
     541: Text { content: "\u{a0}" }
     542: EndParagraph
     543: StartParagraph { alignment: Some(Justify), id: None }
     544: Text { content: "\u{a0}" }
     545: EndParagraph
     546: StartParagraph { alignment: Some(Center), id: None }
     547: StartTextStyle { kind: Bold, id: None }
     548: StartTextStyle { kind: TextColor(Rgb { b: 153, g: 102, r: 0 }), id: None }
     549: Text { content: "Funding History" }
     550: EndTextStyle
     551: EndTextStyle
     552: EndParagraph
     553: StartParagraph { alignment: Some(Justify), id: None }
     554: Text { content: " " }
     555: EndParagraph
     556: StartParagraph { alignment: Some(Justify), id: None }
     557: Text { content: "The RECA Trust Fund was subject to discretionary appropriations from FY 1992 to FY 2001.  Following enactment of the 2000 Amendments, the appropriation became insufficient to meet the increase in the number of claims deemed eligible for compensation.  In 2002, Congress addressed the problem within the Department of Defense Authorization Act for FY 2002, which established annual funding against mandatory spending caps.  However, by 2003 the increased rate of new claim filings and approvals proved the caps to be inadequate, and a funding shortfall ensued.  Working in close coordination, the appropriators and authorizers effectively devised legislative solutions to the funding problems.  The following statutes ensure that" }
     558: Text { content: " " }
     559: Text { content: "all compensable RECA claims will be fully funded throughout the life of the Program.     " }
     560: EndParagraph
     561: StartParagraph { alignment: Some(Justify), id: None }
     562: Text { content: "  " }
     563: EndParagraph
     564: EndOrderedListItem
     565: StartUnorderedListItem { id: Some("28"), level: 0, style_type: Disc }
     566: StartParagraph { alignment: Some(Justify), id: None }
     567: Text { content: "The Consolidated Appropriations Act for 2005 contained language that made funding for the RECA Trust Fund mandatory and indefinite beginning in FY 2006.  Henceforth, the Fund has exclusively paid Section 4 claimants (downwinders and on-site participants)." }
     568: EndParagraph
     569: StartParagraph { alignment: Some(Justify), id: None }
     570: EndParagraph
     571: EndUnorderedListItem
     572: StartUnorderedListItem { id: Some("25"), level: 0, style_type: Disc }
     573: StartParagraph { alignment: Some(Justify), id: None }
     574: Text { content: "The National Defense Authorization Act for FY 2005 requires that RECA Section 5 claimants (uranium miners, millers, and ore transporters) be paid out of the Energy Employees Occupational Illness Compensation Fund.  " }
     575: EndParagraph
     576: StartParagraph { alignment: Some(Center), id: None }
     577: EndParagraph
     578: StartParagraph { alignment: Some(Center), id: None }
     579: StartTextStyle { kind: Bold, id: None }
     580: StartTextStyle { kind: TextColor(Rgb { b: 153, g: 102, r: 0 }), id: None }
     581: Text { content: "Claim Statistics" }
     582: EndTextStyle
     583: EndTextStyle
     584: EndParagraph
     585: StartParagraph { alignment: Some(Justify), id: None }
     586: EndParagraph
     587: StartParagraph { alignment: Some(Justify), id: None }
     588: Text { content: "Over the past 15 years, more than 26,700 claims have been filed with the Program.  Approximately 70 percent of the claims that have been adjudicated were approved.  In FY 2006, total RECA awards over the life of the Program topped $1 billion.    " }
     589: EndParagraph
     590: StartParagraph { alignment: Some(Justify), id: None }
     591: EndParagraph
     592: StartParagraph { alignment: Some(Justify), id: None }
     593: Text { content: "Prior to enactment of the 2000 Amendments, receipts had tapered off and approximately 43 percent of claims were approved.  Following enactment, the number of claims filed and the portion found to be eligible increased sharply.  By the end of FY 2002, the workload had increased more than fivefold to 6,349 claims, and the average approval rate had increased to about 80 percent.  The chart below shows how the 2000 Amendments changed the distribution of awards across the claimant categories.  The changes in statutory requirements for compensation resulted in greater numbers of qualifying claimants, especially downwinders." }
     594: EndParagraph
     595: StartParagraph { alignment: Some(Center), id: None }
     596: Image { alt: Some("This is a bar chart showing that since FY 1999, the distribution of approved RECA claims has shifted from being predominantly uranium miner claims to predominantly downwinder claims.  "), decorative: false, id: None, title: None, asset: AssetDescriptor { asset_id: "zip://word/media/image2.emf", content_type: "image/x-emf", bytes: 33620, sha256: "61dd726a5c030e75c7b2963355a3158bbc5bba1920959ee935684c13d3ceb030" } }
     597: EndParagraph
     598: StartParagraph { alignment: Some(Justify), id: None }
     599: Text { content: "The table on page seven displays actual data from FY 2004 through FY 2007 and projections through FY 2009.  Overall, the number of claims filed has been decreasing – there were 25 percent fewer new claims in FY 2007 than in FY 2004.  A decline in awards is also expected – the value of awards in FY 2009 is projected to be 40 percent less than in FY 2004.  The projections are based on the following assumptions: 1) the number of new claims filed will decline gradually; 2) the approval rate will not increase significantly; and 3) there will be no substantive statutory changes.    " }
     600: EndParagraph
     601: StartParagraph { alignment: Some(Justify), id: None }
     602: EndParagraph
     603: StartParagraph { alignment: Some(Justify), id: None }
     604: Text { content: "The Civil Division’s projections for claim filings, adjudications, and awards have been reviewed by the Department of Justice’s independent auditor since FY 2005.  Using historic data, a model has been developed to estimate the contingent liability associated with RECA awards through the sunset of the program in FY 2022.  Each year, the Civil Division has received a clean audit opinion on this methodology and the resulting liability estimates.   " }
     605: EndParagraph
     606: StartParagraph { alignment: Some(Justify), id: None }
     607: EndParagraph
     608: StartParagraph { alignment: Some(Center), id: None }
     609: StartTextStyle { kind: Bold, id: None }
     610: Text { content: "Performance, Resources, and Strategies" }
     611: EndTextStyle
     612: EndParagraph
     613: StartParagraph { alignment: None, id: None }
     614: EndParagraph
     615: StartParagraph { alignment: Some(Justify), id: None }
     616: StartTextStyle { kind: Bold, id: None }
     617: StartTextStyle { kind: TextColor(Rgb { b: 153, g: 102, r: 0 }), id: None }
     618: Text { content: "Performance Plan and Report for Outcomes" }
     619: EndTextStyle
     620: EndTextStyle
     621: EndParagraph
     622: StartParagraph { alignment: Some(Justify), id: None }
     623: EndParagraph
     624: StartParagraph { alignment: Some(Justify), id: None }
     625: Text { content: "The Radiation Exposure Compensation Program supports Goal 2 of the Department of Justice’s Strategic Plan, specifically Objective 2.7:  “Vigorously enforce and represent the interests of the United States in all matters over which the Department has jurisdiction.”  " }
     626: EndParagraph
     627: StartParagraph { alignment: Some(Justify), id: None }
     628: EndParagraph
     629: StartParagraph { alignment: Some(Justify), id: None }
     630: Text { content: "The Program’s primary objective is to implement civil justice reform initiatives to resolve categories of claims for which traditional litigation has proven ineffective and to administer compensation programs enacted by Congress that offer non-litigation solutions for radiation exposure claimants." }
     631: EndParagraph
     632: StartParagraph { alignment: Some(Justify), id: None }
     633: EndParagraph
     634: StartParagraph { alignment: Some(Justify), id: None }
     635: StartTextStyle { kind: Bold, id: None }
     636: StartTextStyle { kind: TextColor(Rgb { b: 153, g: 102, r: 0 }), id: None }
     637: Text { content: "Strategies to Accomplish Outcomes" }
     638: EndTextStyle
     639: EndTextStyle
     640: EndParagraph
     641: StartParagraph { alignment: Some(Justify), id: None }
     642: EndParagraph
     643: StartParagraph { alignment: Some(Justify), id: None }
     644: Text { content: "The Program will employ the following strategies to accomplish this mission:" }
     645: EndParagraph
     646: StartParagraph { alignment: Some(Justify), id: None }
     647: EndParagraph
     648: EndUnorderedListItem
     649: StartUnorderedListItem { id: Some("15"), level: 0, style_type: Disc }
     650: StartParagraph { alignment: None, id: None }
     651: Text { content: "\t" }
     652: Text { content: "\t" }
     653: Text { content: "Hire skilled claims examiners to conduct the initial review of claims, freeing the Program attorneys to conclude the adjudication and render the final determination." }
     654: EndParagraph
     655: StartParagraph { alignment: Some(Justify), id: None }
     656: EndParagraph
     657: EndUnorderedListItem
     658: StartUnorderedListItem { id: Some("15"), level: 0, style_type: Disc }
     659: StartParagraph { alignment: None, id: None }
     660: Text { content: "\t" }
     661: Text { content: "\t" }
     662: Text { content: "Access external data sources, such as the Social Security Administration, the National Institute for Occupational Safety and Health, the Public Health Service, and state cancer and tumor registries to assist claimants in securing the necessary documentation in support of their claims." }
     663: EndParagraph
     664: StartParagraph { alignment: Some(Justify), id: None }
     665: EndParagraph
     666: EndUnorderedListItem
     667: StartUnorderedListItem { id: Some("15"), level: 0, style_type: Disc }
     668: StartParagraph { alignment: None, id: None }
     669: Text { content: "\t" }
     670: Text { content: "\t" }
     671: Text { content: "Coordinate with the Department of Labor’s (DOL) Energy Employees Occupational Illness Compensation Program to ensure that eligible Section 5 RECA claimants receive compensation in a timely manner.  This includes review of RECA claimant files to determine eligibility pursuant to the Energy Employees Occupational Illness Compensation Program Act." }
     672: EndParagraph
     673: StartParagraph { alignment: None, id: None }
     674: Text { content: "\t" }
     675: EndParagraph
     676: EndUnorderedListItem
     677: StartUnorderedListItem { id: Some("15"), level: 0, style_type: Disc }
     678: StartParagraph { alignment: None, id: None }
     679: Text { content: "\t" }
     680: Text { content: "\t" }
     681: Text { content: "Brief Members of Congress and their staffs as requested; provide information to Members and the public in an open, timely, and complete manner.  " }
     682: EndParagraph
     683: EndUnorderedListItem
     684: StartUnorderedListItem { id: Some("15"), level: 0, style_type: Disc }
     685: StartParagraph { alignment: None, id: None }
     686: Text { content: "\t" }
     687: Text { content: "\t" }
     688: Text { content: "Coordinate with the Department of Health and Human Services’ Radiation Exposure Screening and Education Program to assist grantees in providing relevant information on the RECA Program to individuals screened for disease in the affected geographic regions." }
     689: EndParagraph
     690: StartParagraph { alignment: None, id: None }
     691: Text { content: "\t" }
     692: EndParagraph
     693: EndUnorderedListItem
     694: StartUnorderedListItem { id: Some("15"), level: 0, style_type: Disc }
     695: StartParagraph { alignment: None, id: None }
     696: Text { content: "\t" }
     697: Text { content: "\t" }
     698: Text { content: "Use a toll-free phone line and website to communicate with claimants." }
     699: EndParagraph
     700: StartParagraph { alignment: Some(Justify), id: None }
     701: EndParagraph
     702: EndUnorderedListItem
     703: StartUnorderedListItem { id: Some("15"), level: 0, style_type: Disc }
     704: StartParagraph { alignment: None, id: None }
     705: Text { content: "\t" }
     706: Text { content: "\t" }
     707: Text { content: "Conduct " }
     708: Text { content: "outreach by traveling to areas with populations of potential claimants and participat" }
     709: Text { content: "ing" }
     710: Text { content: " in workshops held by congressional delegations for their constituents.\u{a0} " }
     711: Text { content: "Last" }
     712: Text { content: " year, staff members traveled to the Navajo Indian Reservation to meet with tribal officials" }
     713: Text { content: " " }
     714: Text { content: "and representatives from" }
     715: Text { content: " the Navajo Nation, Office of Navajo Uranium Workers, and" }
     716: Text { content: " the Indian Health Service to discuss initiatives to increase efficiencies in claims adjudication.\u{a0} Also, Program staff members attended town" }
     717: Text { content: " " }
     718: Text { content: "hall meetings with\u{a0}D" }
     719: Text { content: "O" }
     720: Text { content: "L officials in Shiprock" }
     721: Text { content: " and Grant" }
     722: Text { content: ", New Mexico" }
     723: Text { content: "; Grand Junction, Colorado; Moab, Utah;" }
     724: Text { content: " and Kayenta, Arizona, to assist in providing information regarding D" }
     725: Text { content: "OL " }
     726: Text { content: "and RECA benefits." }
     727: EndParagraph
     728: StartParagraph { alignment: Some(Justify), id: None }
     729: EndParagraph
     730: StartParagraph { alignment: None, id: None }
     731: Text { content: "\t" }
     732: Text { content: "\t" }
     733: Text { content: "\t" }
     734: Text { content: "\t" }
     735: Text { content: "\t" }
     736: Text { content: "\t" }
     737: Text { content: "\t" }
     738: Text { content: "\t" }
     739: Text { content: "Results of Program Assessment Rating Tool (PART) Reviews" }
     740: EndParagraph
     741: StartParagraph { alignment: None, id: None }
     742: Text { content: "\t" }
     743: Text { content: "\t" }
     744: Text { content: "\t" }
     745: Text { content: "\t" }
     746: Text { content: "\t" }
     747: Text { content: "\t" }
     748: Text { content: "\t" }
     749: Text { content: "\t" }
     750: EndParagraph
     751: StartParagraph { alignment: None, id: None }
     752: Text { content: "\t" }
     753: Text { content: "\t" }
     754: Text { content: "\t" }
     755: Text { content: "\t" }
     756: Text { content: "\t" }
     757: Text { content: "\t" }
     758: Text { content: "\t" }
     759: Text { content: "\t" }
     760: Text { content: "The RECA Program was evaluated with the Office of Management and Budget’s Program Assessment Rating Tool (PART) during FY 2006.  The Program received a rating of “Adequate.”  This rating describes a program that needs to set more ambitious goals, achieve better results, improve accountability, or strengthen its management practices.  " }
     761: EndParagraph
     762: StartParagraph { alignment: None, id: None }
     763: Text { content: "\t" }
     764: Text { content: "\t" }
     765: Text { content: "\t" }
     766: Text { content: "\t" }
     767: Text { content: "\t" }
     768: Text { content: "\t" }
     769: Text { content: "\t" }
     770: Text { content: "\t" }
     771: EndParagraph
     772: StartParagraph { alignment: None, id: None }
     773: Text { content: "\t" }
     774: Text { content: "\t" }
     775: Text { content: "\t" }
     776: Text { content: "\t" }
     777: Text { content: "\t" }
     778: Text { content: "\t" }
     779: Text { content: "\t" }
     780: Text { content: "\t" }
     781: Text { content: "OMB’s findings include:" }
     782: EndParagraph
     783: StartParagraph { alignment: None, id: None }
     784: Text { content: "\t" }
     785: Text { content: "\t" }
     786: Text { content: "\t" }
     787: Text { content: "\t" }
     788: Text { content: "\t" }
     789: Text { content: "\t" }
     790: Text { content: "\t" }
     791: Text { content: "\t" }
     792: EndParagraph
     793: EndUnorderedListItem
     794: StartUnorderedListItem { id: Some("29"), level: 0, style_type: Disc }
     795: StartParagraph { alignment: None, id: None }
     796: Text { content: "\t" }
     797: Text { content: "\t" }
     798: Text { content: "\t" }
     799: Text { content: "\t" }
     800: Text { content: "\t" }
     801: Text { content: "\t" }
     802: Text { content: "\t" }
     803: Text { content: "\t" }
     804: Text { content: "\t" }
     805: Text { content: "The Program has developed ambitious annual and long-term goals focusing on outcomes that meaningfully reflect the purpose of the Program." }
     806: StartTextStyle { kind: Bold, id: None }
     807: Text { content: " " }
     808: EndTextStyle
     809: StartTextStyle { kind: Bold, id: None }
     810: Text { content: " " }
     811: EndTextStyle
     812: Text { content: "However, the " }
     813: Text { content: "P" }
     814: Text { content: "rogram must ensure that partners are committed to achieving annual and long-term goals" }
     815: Text { content: "." }
     816: EndParagraph
     817: StartParagraph { alignment: None, id: None }
     818: Text { content: "\t" }
     819: Text { content: "\t" }
     820: Text { content: "\t" }
     821: Text { content: "\t" }
     822: Text { content: "\t" }
     823: Text { content: "\t" }
     824: Text { content: "\t" }
     825: Text { content: "\t" }
     826: EndParagraph
     827: EndUnorderedListItem
     828: StartUnorderedListItem { id: Some("29"), level: 0, style_type: Disc }
     829: StartParagraph { alignment: None, id: None }
     830: Text { content: "\t" }
     831: Text { content: "\t" }
     832: Text { content: "\t" }
     833: Text { content: "\t" }
     834: Text { content: "\t" }
     835: Text { content: "\t" }
     836: Text { content: "\t" }
     837: Text { content: "\t" }
     838: Text { content: "\t" }
     839: Text { content: "The Program" }
     840: Text { content: "’" }
     841: Text { content: "s statutory scheme contains flaws with respect to some of its claimant categories." }
     842: StartTextStyle { kind: Bold, id: None }
     843: Text { content: " " }
     844: EndTextStyle
     845: StartTextStyle { kind: Bold, id: None }
     846: Text { content: " " }
     847: EndTextStyle
     848: Text { content: "Although the statute is founded on the scientifically-based association between exposure and illness for occupationally exposed uranium workers, the same is not true for other claimant categories. " }
     849: EndParagraph
     850: StartParagraph { alignment: None, id: None }
     851: Text { content: "\t" }
     852: Text { content: "\t" }
     853: Text { content: "\t" }
     854: Text { content: "\t" }
     855: Text { content: "\t" }
     856: Text { content: "\t" }
     857: Text { content: "\t" }
     858: Text { content: "\t" }
     859: EndParagraph
     860: StartParagraph { alignment: None, id: None }
     861: Text { content: "\t" }
     862: Text { content: "\t" }
     863: Text { content: "\t" }
     864: Text { content: "\t" }
     865: Text { content: "\t" }
     866: Text { content: "\t" }
     867: Text { content: "\t" }
     868: Text { content: "\t" }
     869: Text { content: "The Department of Justice will take the following actions to improve the RECA Program’s performance:" }
     870: EndParagraph
     871: StartParagraph { alignment: None, id: None }
     872: Text { content: "\t" }
     873: Text { content: "\t" }
     874: Text { content: "\t" }
     875: Text { content: "\t" }
     876: Text { content: "\t" }
     877: Text { content: "\t" }
     878: Text { content: "\t" }
     879: Text { content: "\t" }
     880: EndParagraph
     881: EndUnorderedListItem
     882: StartUnorderedListItem { id: Some("30"), level: 0, style_type: Disc }
     883: StartParagraph { alignment: None, id: None }
     884: Text { content: "\t" }
     885: Text { content: "\t" }
     886: Text { content: "\t" }
     887: Text { content: "\t" }
     888: Text { content: "\t" }
     889: Text { content: "\t" }
     890: Text { content: "\t" }
     891: Text { content: "\t" }
     892: Text { content: "\t" }
     893: Text { content: "Ensur" }
     894: Text { content: "e" }
     895: Text { content: " Program partners are expressly committed to achieving the stated annual and long-term performance goals of the Program" }
     896: Text { content: "." }
     897: EndParagraph
     898: StartParagraph { alignment: None, id: None }
     899: Text { content: "\t" }
     900: Text { content: "\t" }
     901: Text { content: "\t" }
     902: Text { content: "\t" }
     903: Text { content: "\t" }
     904: Text { content: "\t" }
     905: Text { content: "\t" }
     906: Text { content: "\t" }
     907: Text { content: "\t" }
     908: Text { content: "\t" }
     909: EndParagraph
     910: EndUnorderedListItem
     911: StartUnorderedListItem { id: Some("30"), level: 0, style_type: Disc }
     912: StartParagraph { alignment: None, id: None }
     913: Text { content: "\t" }
     914: Text { content: "\t" }
     915: Text { content: "\t" }
     916: Text { content: "\t" }
     917: Text { content: "\t" }
     918: Text { content: "\t" }
     919: Text { content: "\t" }
     920: Text { content: "\t" }
     921: Text { content: "\t" }
     922: Text { content: "Develop a plan to tie resources to specific performance measures" }
     923: Text { content: "." }
     924: EndParagraph
     925: StartParagraph { alignment: None, id: None }
     926: Text { content: "\t" }
     927: Text { content: "\t" }
     928: Text { content: "\t" }
     929: Text { content: "\t" }
     930: Text { content: "\t" }
     931: Text { content: "\t" }
     932: Text { content: "\t" }
     933: Text { content: "\t" }
     934: EndParagraph
     935: EndUnorderedListItem
     936: StartUnorderedListItem { id: Some("30"), level: 0, style_type: Disc }
     937: StartParagraph { alignment: None, id: None }
     938: Text { content: "\t" }
     939: Text { content: "\t" }
     940: Text { content: "\t" }
     941: Text { content: "\t" }
     942: Text { content: "\t" }
     943: Text { content: "\t" }
     944: Text { content: "\t" }
     945: Text { content: "\t" }
     946: Text { content: "\t" }
     947: Text { content: "Monitor" }
     948: Text { content: " " }
     949: Text { content: "the activities of the National Academy of Sciences and " }
     950: Text { content: "similar" }
     951: Text { content: " organizations that are studying the Act" }
     952: Text { content: "’" }
     953: Text { content: "s eligibility criteria. " }
     954: EndParagraph
     955: StartParagraph { alignment: None, id: None }
     956: Text { content: "\t" }
     957: Text { content: "\t" }
     958: Text { content: "\t" }
